highlights:
I'm facing an issue in a project I'm currently working on. I have a series of modal dialogs made with CSS (display: fixed) that are hidden by default with display: none;. In Chrome, when opening these dialogs, all the text is invisible (I can select it, but it is not visible). Using the inspector, I can change for example its font-weight and the text will then be visible, even when reverting to its original font weight. I'm using a custom font (MuseoSans) imported with the following CSS code:
...
```
@font-face {
    font-family: "MuseoSans";
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 100;
    src: url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.eot?") format("eot"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.woff") format("woff"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.ttf") format("truetype"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.svg#MuseoSans") format("svg"); }
...
@font-face {
    font-family: "MuseoSans";
    font-style: normal;
    font-weight: 300;
    src: url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.eot?") format("eot"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.woff") format("woff"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.ttf") format("truetype"), url("../fonts/MuseoSans_100-webfont.svg#MuseoSans") format("svg"); }
...
I found that if in these dialogs I switch to font-family: Verdana; for example, text will be always visible. Any ideas? I could only reproduce this behavior in Google Chrome (52.0.2743.116 (Build oficial) m (32 bits)).
...
EDIT: found out it works as it should if the font size and weight are rendered in a visible place prior to opening the modal dialog.
...
- **Rising Concupiscence**: It seems the issue only occurs with Museo Sans (at least). I just replaced it with Open Sans (same mixin and filenames to import them using CSS) and can't reproduce the problem. I generated both webfonts from the Font Squirrel generator. I know I should post an example but I assume I can't create a jsbin that uses MuseoSans as it's a propietary font. I did double check color, background and such where right, of course. Again, using the inspector to just change font-size, weight or any other font property, it renders fine even after undoing these changes (problem reoccurs after browser reload).
...
- **Mike 'Pomax' Kamermans**: No idea, you're not really showing enough code to tell, nor a jsbin or something that reproduces this outside your (presumably large) codebase, so: did you remember to give your dialog explicit CSS `background-color` and `color` values?
